# Multi-delogo Image Presets Configuration
# =========================================
#
# Define image presets here for quick replacement of logos/watermarks.
# Each preset includes: ID, display name, image file, position & dimensions.
#
# FILE LOCATION (searched in order):
#   1. Same folder as your .mdl project file: image_presets.conf
#   2. Same folder as your video file: image_presets.conf  
#   3. Home directory: ~/.multi-delogo-presets.conf
#
# =========================================
# FORMAT:
# id|display_name|image_path|position_type|p1|p2|p3|p4
#
# POSITION TYPES:
# =========================================
#
# 1. ABS (Absolute) - Exact pixel coordinates
#    ------------------------------------------------
#    Format: ABS|x|y|width|height
#    
#    Parameters:
#      x      = pixels from left edge
#      y      = pixels from top edge  
#      width  = image width in pixels
#      height = image height in pixels
#    
#    Example for 1920x1080 video, logo at top-right:
#    logo1|Channel Logo|logo.png|ABS|1800|20|100|60
#
#
# 2. MARGIN (Position + Explicit Size) - RECOMMENDED
#    ------------------------------------------------
#    Format: MARGIN|left|top|width|height
#    
#    Parameters:
#      left   = pixels from left edge (x position)
#      top    = pixels from top edge (y position)
#      width  = explicit image width in pixels
#      height = explicit image height in pixels
#    
#    Example: Logo 20px from right, 10px from top, size 100x50
#    For 1920px wide video: left = 1920 - 20 - 100 = 1800
#    logo2|Top Right|logo.png|MARGIN|1800|10|100|50
#
#
# 3. FILL (Margins from all edges) - Auto-calculated size
#    ------------------------------------------------
#    Format: FILL|left|top|right|bottom
#    
#    Parameters:
#      left   = pixels from left edge
#      top    = pixels from top edge
#      right  = pixels from right edge
#      bottom = pixels from bottom edge
#    
#    The image will be scaled to fill the remaining space.
#    
#    Example: Full-width banner, 60px tall at bottom
#    banner|Bottom Banner|banner.png|FILL|0|0|0|60
#    
#    Example: Logo filling top-right corner area
#    corner|Corner Fill|corner.png|FILL|1700|0|0|900
#
# =========================================
# IMAGES DIRECTORY
# =========================================
#
# Set the base directory for your images.
# Relative paths in presets will be relative to this directory.
#
# Example:
images_dir=/home/user/my-project/overlay-images

# =========================================
# PRESET EXAMPLES
# =========================================

# Top-right logo (for 1920x1080 video)
# Position: 1800px from left, 10px from top
# Size: 100x50 pixels
logo_tr|Top Right Logo|logo.png|MARGIN|1800|10|100|50

# Bottom-left watermark
# Position: 20px from left, 710px from top (1080 - 20 - 50 = 710 for bottom alignment)
# Size: 80x50 pixels
watermark_bl|Bottom Left Watermark|watermark.png|MARGIN|20|1010|80|50

# Center sponsor logo
# Position: 860px from left (centered for 100px wide logo: (1920-200)/2)
# Size: 200x100 pixels
sponsor|Sponsor Logo|sponsor.png|MARGIN|860|490|200|100

# Full-width bottom banner (auto-sized)
# Fills entire width, 80px from bottom
banner|Bottom Banner|banner.png|FILL|0|0|0|80

# Absolute position example
# Exact coordinates: x=1150, y=50, size=120x60
channel|Channel Logo|channel_logo.png|ABS|1150|50|120|60

# =========================================
# TIPS
# =========================================
#
# 1. Use PNG images with transparency for best results
#
# 2. MARGIN type is most flexible - you specify exact position and size
#
# 3. FILL type is good for banners that should stretch
#
# 4. Calculate positions for your video resolution:
#    - For right-aligned: left = video_width - margin_right - image_width
#    - For bottom-aligned: top = video_height - margin_bottom - image_height
#
# 5. Test with one preset first before adding many
#
# 6. Keep IDs short and memorable (used in dropdown)
